---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/prose.css';
---

<Layout
  title="License — Derech Tevunos"
  description="The 1742 Hebrew is public domain. Original work in this project is under the Apache License 2.0."
>
  <div class="dt-page">
    <article class="wrap">
      <header>
        <h1 class="dt-page-title">License and attribution</h1>
        <p class="dt-page-description">
          Two different things with two different statuses: the text, and the work built on it.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="dt-prose">
        <div class="callout">
          <p class="callout-label">In short</p>
          <p>
            The Hebrew of the 1742 Amsterdam print is in the <strong>public
            domain</strong> and is not claimed under any license here. Everything
            original in this project — the translation, the labelling system's
            software, the visualization, and this site — is under the
            <strong>Apache License 2.0</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>The Hebrew</h2>
        <p>
          The Hebrew text is the unvocalized 1742 Amsterdam edition of
          <em>Derech Tevunos</em>, as keyed by volunteers at
          <a href="https://benyehuda.org" rel="noopener">Project Ben-Yehuda</a>
          under catalogue ID 53742. It is in the public domain. Nothing in this
          project asserts a copyright over it, and the Apache license below does
          not reach it.
        </p>

        <h2>The English</h2>
        <p>
          The English is a clean-room translation of that Hebrew. Its technical
          vocabulary has been cross-checked against the Diaspora Yeshiva
          translation (Feldheim, 1988/2014) and uses that edition's terms where
          the author prefers them, because they keep enough of the Western-logic
          lexicon to be intelligible to a logician while diverging from the
          Western definitions wherever those do not fit how a sugya actually
          builds and tests a statement.
        </p>
        <p>
          The aim is a <em>functional</em> vocabulary — one that lets a reader,
          or a program, label the moves and statements of a large sugya — not
          doctrinal correctness. Only the terms were taken from that edition;
          the quotations, their citations as printed, and the sense of every
          English sentence are the clean-room translation's own.
        </p>

        <h2>Editorial brackets</h2>
        <p>
          Researching the sources revealed places where the 1742 print's
          quotation or citation differs from the source it cites. Those are
          marked in the English with <code>[ed. …]</code> brackets giving the
          source's reading. The Hebrew print and its translation stand as they
          were; the brackets are the only addition.
        </p>

        <h2>Original work</h2>
        <p>
          Copyright 2026 Alexander Ioffe. Licensed under the Apache License,
          Version 2.0. You may not use this project except in compliance with
          the License. A copy is in the
          <a href="https://github.com/deusaquilus/derech-tevunos/blob/main/LICENSE" rel="noopener">LICENSE</a>
          file, or at
          <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0" rel="noopener">apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
          distributed under the License is distributed on an “AS IS” basis,
          without warranties or conditions of any kind, either express or
          implied. See the License for the specific language governing
          permissions and limitations under it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The full attribution notice is in
          <a href="https://github.com/deusaquilus/derech-tevunos/blob/main/NOTICE" rel="noopener">NOTICE</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .wrap {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 2rem 4rem;
  }

  header { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .wrap { padding: 1.5rem 1rem 3rem; }
  }
</style>
